    <td class=3D"highlight-#e3fcef confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=3D"#=
e3fcef" title=3D"Background color : Light green 35%">
     <p><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;" title=3D"">/users?<em>idp=3Dxx &amp;=
 sourceIdpSub=3D&lt;existing idp subject&gt; &amp; activationDate=3Dxx<br><=
br>
         idp=3Dnbin or blank, means the user needs to be created on Okta NB=
IN tenant.</em></span></p>
     <p><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;" title=3D""><em>idp=3Dnbc means user =
will be onboarded via IIQ and no Okta changes are required.</em></span></p>
     <p><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;" title=3D""><em>idp=3D&lt;anything el=
se&gt; means user will be onboarded via Client IDP and no Okta changes are =
required.<br><br><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;" title=3D"">sourceIdpSub, if=
 specified then create new profile based on exsiting user setup. pre-proces=
sing logic for request body:<br>
          1. lookup existing user attributes for identity and access-contro=
l and create json same as defined for requestBody.<br>
          2. override with attributes in this request's body.<br></span></e=
m></span><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;" title=3D""><em><span style=3D"color=
:#172b4d;" title=3D"">3. set user conf's profile identityLastUpdated to '1-=
1-1970'<br>
          4. set accessProfileSet to true, if featurePackage is set</span><=
/em></span></p>
     <p><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;" title=3D""><em><span style=3D"color:=
#172b4d;" title=3D"">5. update sourceIdpSub attribute on user conf</span></=
em></span></p>
     <p><br></p>
     <ol>
      <li>push updates to Okta for attributes like language <u>only</u> whe=
n idp =3D nbin</li>
      <li>allow updates to identity/personal profile attributes&nbsp;<u>onl=
y</u> when idp =3D nbin</li>
     </ol></td>
