    <td class=3D"highlight-#e3fcef confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=3D"#=
e3fcef" title=3D"Background color : Light green 35%">
     <ul title=3D"">
      <li>200 OK for success</li>
      <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;"><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Cre=
ate :: The idp value (the identitySource configured in Okta) will be used t=
o link a new user to its firm, during creation of a new identity profile. <=
/span><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Lookup&nbsp;</span><strong style=3D"te=
xt-align: left;">idp</strong><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;"><span>&nbsp;</s=
pan>value in firm-configuration for identitySource </span><span style=3D"co=
lor:#172b4d;">and associate the user to this firm.</span></span></li>
      <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;"><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Upd=
ate :: </span></span>
       <ul title=3D"">
        <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">The idp value (the identitySourc=
e configured in Okta) will be updated if it's current value is 'nbin'. If t=
he idp value of user's firm doesn't match this given value, raise an alert =
for IT support.&nbsp;</span></li>
        <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">If the user profile has sourceId=
p then call UF13 for it, using system_token.</span></li>
       </ul></li>
      <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;"><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">res=
ponse to include the firm_id and access_profile_set.</span></span></li>
     </ul></td>
